# Master plan: MQC v0 hardening pass #2

## Status

Second external security review of `socket-level-wrapper-MQC/`.
Source review at
[`README-mqc-2-issues.md`](./README-mqc-2-issues.md).  This file
is the orchestration document for addressing the actionable
findings.

The first hardening pass (`mqc-master.plan`, now trimmed to
deferred-items only) closed the original 12-issue reviewer pack
plus two cross-cutting plans (#6a operational tunables, fork
backpressure) plus the Phase-7 encrypted-mode rewrite.  This
second pass is narrower: 7 actionable findings, ~3 of them
trivial, ~3 substantive, ~1 deferred.

## Triage of the 10 findings

| # | Reviewer claim | Verdict | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Handshake JSON is not length-prefixed | **Agree, fix.** Spec §5.1 requires it; current code reads byte-by-byte via `mqc_read_json_block`. | Phase 1 |
| 2 | Brace-count reader is string-literal-unaware | **Agree, fix.**  `{"k":"}"}` desynchronises framing.  Same fix as #1. | Phase 1 |
| 3 | Cosigner-key TOFU at first contact | **Agree, fix.**  Already tracked as `mtc-keymaster/README-bugsandtodo.md` TODO #9b with design branches in `~/.claude/plans/lets-plan-to-implement-snoopy-rivest.md`. | Phase 5 |
| 4 | Peer pubkey not verified against `subject_public_key_hash` | **Agree, fix — highest severity.**  `extract_pubkey_from_cert` reads PEM from local files, never SHA-256s it and compares.  Anyone with write access to `~/.TPM/peers/<n>/public_key.pem` can substitute the verifier pubkey while keeping the cert hash unchanged → identity-substitution. | Phase 2 |
| 5 | Revocation "mandatory" drops first contact | **Partial disagree.**  Real behavior, but per-(IP, cert) throttle (issue #12) already mitigates the DoS amplification path.  Consider improving the UX but not security-critical. | Phase 6 (may defer) |
| 6 | Transcript binds fields, not raw frame bytes | **Disagree.**  Field-based transcript is by design (spec §6.0), same pattern TLS 1.3 uses.  Reviewer's actual concern is doc clarity around "frame" terminology — fix #1 resolves this. | Closed by Phase 1 |
| 7 | AEAD recv increments seq before auth | **Agree, trivial fix.**  `(*seq)++` at `mqc_common.c:1420` before `wc_AesGcmDecrypt` at line 1425.  Same pattern at `mqc_read:1591`. | Phase 3 |
| 8 | Stale "encrypted is stubbed" comments | **Agree, trivial.**  Three locations: `mqc_internal.h:7`, `mqc.c:15`, `mqc.c:27`. | Phase 4 |
| 9 | `mqc_accept_auto` uses MSG_PEEK + strstr | **Partial agree.**  Workable today (strict-parser fallback catches false positives) but architecturally inelegant.  Fix #1 enables a clean replacement: read framed first frame, parse strict, dispatch from parsed `mode`. | Closed by Phase 1 |
| 10 | No build/test verification | (meta, no action) | n/a |

## End-state vision

After all phases land, MQC v0 has:

- Length-prefixed framing for **every** unit on the wire,
  handshake and data plane alike (spec §5.1 honored).
- No string-literal-unaware framing parser anywhere.
- `mqc_accept_auto` reads a length-prefixed first frame, strict-
  parses it, dispatches from the parsed `mode` field — no
  MSG_PEEK substring search.
- Peer pubkey verified against the cert's
  `subject_public_key_hash` before any signature verification.
  Cache poisoning / local-file substitution can no longer route
  a verifier to an attacker pubkey.
- AEAD receive sequence counter incremented only after a
  successful GCM verify.
- Documentation says what the code does (no "stubbed encrypted
  mode" claims in a tree where encrypted mode is shipped).
- Cosigner-key bootstrap is no longer pure TOFU — operator-
  pinned out-of-band, with a verifiable enrollment path
  (snoopy-rivest plan branches).

The protocol stays at draft-page-mqc-protocol-**00**; spec edits
land within that draft.  Same flag-day deployment model as the
first pass — server and clients always upgrade together.

---

## Phase 1 — Length-prefixed handshake frames (one flag-day cutover)

Closes findings #1, #2, #6, #9 — all of which derive from the
same design choice (or oversight) about handshake framing.

**What changes on the wire:**

Pre-Phase-1 handshake (Phase-1-of-mqc-2, that is — the original
mqc-1 Phase 1 was different):

```
client → server:  raw JSON bytes, no length prefix, read by
                   mqc_read_json_block byte-by-byte
```

Post-Phase-1:

```
client → server:  4-byte big-endian length prefix
                || JSON bytes (exactly as many as the prefix says)
```

Same shape spec §5.1 already mandates for data-plane frames.
The handshake JSON content itself is unchanged — just the
framing wrapper.

**Code changes:**

- `mqc_common.c`:
  - New `mqc_write_handshake_frame(fd, buf, len)`: writes
    `htonl(len)` + `len` bytes via `mqc_write_all`.
  - New `mqc_read_handshake_frame(fd, buf, max_len)`: reads
    4 bytes, decodes length, validates against
    `mqc-max-handshake-bytes`, reads exactly that many bytes
    via `mqc_read_all`.  Returns the body length on success,
    -1 on error.  Replaces every call site of
    `mqc_read_json_block`.
  - **Delete** `mqc_read_json_block` and its forward decl in
    `mqc_internal.h`.  Three call sites currently reference
    it; all become `mqc_read_handshake_frame`.

- `mqc_clear.c` (both bodies): replace each
  `mqc_write_all(fd, json_buf, json_len)` followed by send
  with `mqc_write_handshake_frame(fd, json_buf, json_len)`.
  Replace each `mqc_read_json_block(fd, json_buf, sizeof(json_buf))`
  with `mqc_read_handshake_frame(fd, json_buf, sizeof(json_buf))`.

- `mqc_encrypted.c` (both bodies + both phase-1 frames):
  same replacement pattern.  Phase-2 already uses `mqc_enc_send`
  / `mqc_enc_recv` which are length-prefixed; no change there.

- `mqc.c` `mqc_accept_auto`:
  - Drop the MSG_PEEK substring search.
  - Read the length-prefixed first frame via the new
    `mqc_read_handshake_frame`.
  - `mqc_json_parse_strict` it.
  - Read the `mode` field via `mqc_json_get_string_exact`
    matching against `"clear"` or `"encrypted"`.
  - Dispatch to `mqc_accept_clear_post_with_buf(ctx, fd,
    client_ip, json_buf, json_len, parsed_obj)` or the
    encrypted equivalent.  **Both sub-handlers must take the
    already-read first frame as input** (parallel to the
    existing `_post` factoring) — this is the load-bearing
    refactor of Phase 1.

- `mqc_clear.c` / `mqc_encrypted.c`: refactor each `_post`
  variant so that the FIRST `mqc_read_handshake_frame` call
  is now optional (skipped if the caller passed the
  already-read first frame).  Cleanest API: introduce
  `mqc_accept_clear_with_first_frame(ctx, fd, client_ip,
  buf, len, parsed_obj)` and have `mqc_accept_clear_post`
  be a thin wrapper that reads the first frame itself then
  calls the new function.  Same for encrypted.

- `mtc-keymaster/tools/c/attack-port-8446.c`: every existing
  attack that sends raw JSON now needs a 4-byte length prefix
  prepended.  Update `send_json` (currently a thin wrapper
  around `attack_raw`) to prepend `htonl(strlen(body))`.  The
  raw-bytes attacks (`a_random*`, `a_all_zeros`, etc.) stay
  unchanged — they're testing what happens when the framing
  itself is malformed.  Add new attacks targeting the
  length-prefix layer specifically:
    - `p3d-frame-len-zero`        (length prefix = 0)
    - `p3d-frame-len-too-large`   (length prefix > max-handshake-bytes)
    - `p3d-frame-len-truncated`   (only 2 bytes of the length
                                   prefix, then close)
    - `p3d-frame-tail-bytes`      (length prefix says N, send N
                                   bytes of valid JSON, then keep
                                   sending more bytes — server
                                   should consume exactly N and
                                   ignore the rest until the next
                                   frame boundary)

**Spec changes:**

- §5.1: tighten the existing "every unit … is a length-prefixed
  frame" sentence to remove any ambiguity.  Add a note that
  the handshake JSON's `payload length` excludes the length
  prefix itself (matches data-plane convention).
- §6 / §7: each describes the handshake JSON content; add a
  one-line note that frame layout is per §5.1.  No JSON
  content change.
- Appendix A worked example: prepend the 4-byte length prefix
  to each ClientHello / ServerHello bytes shown.  Length
  numbers will need recalculating from a fresh capture.

**Cutover:**

Single flag-day commit (server + all clients).  Same pattern
as the original Phase 1.  Smoke test: `show-tpm --verify`
(clear) and `show-tpm --verify --encrypted` both succeed
post-restart.

**Exit criteria:**

- Zero-warning build.
- `make -f Makefile.tools test-mqc-all` passes 4/4.
- `mqc_read_json_block` is gone from the tree (`grep -r
  mqc_read_json_block` returns nothing).
- A handshake JSON containing a literal `}` inside a string
  value (e.g., `"signature":"abcd..}xx.."`) is correctly
  framed and parsed — add a regression test.
- attack-port-8446 includes the new `p3d-frame-*` probes; all
  produce clean rejections in the journal.

