## Phase 3 — AEAD seq increment after verify (issue #7)

Closes finding #7.  Trivial.

**What changes:**

In `mqc_common.c` `mqc_enc_recv` (line 1420) and `mqc_read`
(line 1591), move the `(*seq)++` / `conn->recv_seq++` line to
**after** the `wc_AesGcmDecrypt` call returns success.  On
failure, leave `recv_seq` untouched (the connection will be
torn down anyway, but the spec says "increments on success"
and behavior should match).

**Spec changes:** none — §9.2 already says "AEAD-decrypts with
the matching AAD, increments `recv_seq` on success."  This
brings code in line with spec wording.

**Tests:**

- Aggregate suite still passes (no behavior change for the
  happy path).
- Add an attack-port-8446 probe that sends a tampered AEAD
  frame; verify the reject log line names the correct sequence
  (the one that was being checked, not the one after).

