## Phase 5 — Cosigner-key bootstrap hardening (issue #3)

Closes finding #3.  Picks up the existing TODO #9b design
captured in
`/home/ubuntu/.claude/plans/lets-plan-to-implement-snoopy-rivest.md`.

**Out of scope for this master plan:** the actual design.  The
snoopy-rivest plan has two branches (leaf-bootstrap path,
CA-bootstrap path) that are themselves substantial — pick one
and write a per-branch plan when ready.

**Recommended path:** start with the leaf-bootstrap branch
because it has a natural OOB channel (the operator-issued
enrollment nonce) that the CA-bootstrap branch lacks.

**Phase 5 of THIS plan is just the trigger:** copy the
snoopy-rivest plan branches into a new
`mqc-2-issue-tofu.plan` in this directory, decide on
ordering, and proceed.

---

## Phase 6 — Revocation first-contact UX (issue #5, may defer)

Closes finding #5.  Current behavior (cache miss → fetch +
write cache + return failure → caller retries) is correct but
operationally surprising — every fresh peer gets a "first
connection always fails" experience.

**Possible improvement:** complete the handshake on the first
contact when the freshly-fetched revocation status is "not
revoked," instead of dropping.  This requires plumbing the
fetched status through the rest of `mqc_peer_verify` instead
of setting it aside for the next call.

**Decision deferred.**  May land if Phase 1+2 expose
documentation / regression hooks that make this easy.  May
defer indefinitely if the per-(IP, cert) throttle from #12
proves to fully mitigate the DoS concern (it has, in practice,
during Phase-4 stress testing).

---

## Phase ordering

```
Phase 1  ─►  Phase 2  ─►  Phase 3  ─►  Phase 4  ─►  Phase 5
flag-day     pubkey-      seq-fix      doc          TOFU
framing      hash-bind    (1 line)     cleanup      design
                                                    (snoopy-
                                                     rivest)

                                       Phase 6 (deferred)
                                       revocation UX
```

Phase 1 first because it's a flag day — bundling other changes
into it is operationally cheap (one cutover window).  Phase 2
right after because it's the highest-severity finding but is
wire-quiet (can ship any time).  Phases 3 + 4 are
trivial cleanup.  Phase 5 is its own substantial project.
Phase 6 may never land.

## Suggested commit boundaries

| Commit | Phase | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| `mqc-2-1` | Phase 1 | Length-prefixed handshake frames + drop brace-count reader + auto-detect refactor + p3d-frame-* attacks + spec §5.1/§6/§7/Appendix A edits |
| `mqc-2-2` | Phase 2 | Pubkey-hash binding in extract_pubkey_from_cert + regression test + spec §10.2 / §12.11 edits |
| `mqc-2-3` | Phase 3 | AEAD recv seq increment after verify (mqc_common.c lines 1420 + 1591) |
| `mqc-2-4` | Phase 4 | Stale "stubbed" comments in mqc_internal.h:7, mqc.c:15, mqc.c:27 |
| `mqc-2-5` | Phase 5 | Triggers a new `mqc-2-issue-tofu.plan` (leaf-bootstrap branch first) |
| `mqc-2-6` | (deferred) | Revocation first-contact UX (only if motivated) |

## Verification milestones

- After Phase 1: `make -f Makefile.tools test-mqc-all` 4/4
  with the new framing.  attack-port-8446 includes p3d-frame-*
  attacks; all produce clean rejections.  show-tpm --verify
  and show-tpm --verify --encrypted both succeed.
- After Phase 2: attempting a connection with a corrupted
  `~/.TPM/peers/<n>/public_key.pem` produces
  `PUBKEY_HASH_MISMATCH` and aborts.
- After Phase 3: aggregate suite unchanged.  No measurable
  perf change.
- After Phase 4: `grep -rn "stubbed encrypted\|encrypted.*stub\|Phase 7 commit 2"
  socket-level-wrapper-MQC/` returns only the historical
  comments in mqc_encrypted.c's file header (which is
  retrospective, not stale).
- Phase 5: separate plan, separate exit criteria.

## Out of scope (across all phases)

- Replacing JSON wire format with CBOR / TLV.  JSON is
  workable; the framing fix in Phase 1 makes it spec-compliant.
- Revisiting the field-based vs raw-bytes transcript decision
  (reviewer finding #6).  Field-based is intentional and
  TLS-1.3-aligned.
- Anything from the original mqc-master.plan's "Out of scope"
  list (those remain deferred).
